 "texts": {
  "history": [
   {
    "text": "The name derives from the Sanskrit jval for \"shine\", the Teutonic word gulth for \"shining metal\", and the Anglo-Saxon gold of unknown origin. The symbol Au derives from the Latin aurum, for Aurora, the goddess of dawn. Gold was known and highly valued in prehistoric times.",
    "source": "ciaaw"
